ght's behavior when [tool.uv].required-version is absent or `uv --version` output is unparseable (fail with a clear message vs fall through to existing handler).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8746,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["New parsing/comparison step introduced before uv venv","No stated fallback if required-version is absent or uv --version output cannot be parsed"],"finding":"The preflight parses `uv --version` and reads `[tool.uv].required-version` from pyproject.toml, but the plan does not specify behavior when either is absent or unparseable (e.g. missing required-version key, unexpected uv version output).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f91c368ee89e3e771","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'compares the selected uv executable/version with the repository exact required version'","norm_id":"n43e5aa8a3110f745","priority":0.0754,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future pyproject without [tool.uv].required-version runs make worktree","uv changes its --version output format"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the bespoke uv-version preflight against the lighter alternative of classifying/surfacing uv's own `required-version` refusal (which uv already emits) instead of re-implementing the version comparison in Make/shell.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Context: 'uv venv correctly refused the mismatch, but the Makefile catch-all handler reported that Python 3.12 was unavailable' — the misclassification, not the detection, is the defect","uv natively enforces [tool.uv] required-version and emits a refusal; the fix could inspect/surface that refusal rather than duplicate the comparison","required-version parsing already exists in scripts/check_uv_pin.py:_required_version and .github/actions/setup-uv/action.yml — a third bespoke parser/comparator in Make is NIH"],"finding":"The plan adds a bespoke Make/shell uv-version preflight (parse required-version, parse `uv --version`, compare) even though uv itself already performs this comparison and refuses the mismatch — the plan states 'uv venv correctly refused the mismatch'. The lighter alternative of surfacing/classifying uv's own required-version refusal (instead of swallowing it in the catch-all handler at Makefile:200-208) is not weighed. Re-implementing uv's native version-comparison risks divergence from uv's own specifier semantics (exact vs range parsing already handled once in scripts/check_uv_pin.py).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0c000920dbb1626f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Add a preflight that compares the selected uv executable/version with the repository exact required version before uv venv'","norm_id":"nb60456a32f4986bf","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future uv changes its version-specifier handling and the shell preflight diverges from uv's own enforcement","Maintenance cost of a hand-rolled version comparison in Makefile shell for a check uv already performs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the bespoke uv-version preflight against the lighter alternative of surfacing (not swallowing) uv's own `required-version` refusal in the venv recipe — given uv already reads the pin and reports actual-vs-required — or adopt that alternative.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4289,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["pyproject.toml:353-354: 'uv reads required-version itself, so a local uv that differs now fails fast with `Update uv by running uv self update 0.12.7`. That is intended'","Makefile:200-208: the `uv venv ... || { ... }` catch-all prints the 'could not provision .venv on Python <v>' + 'uv python install' text, overwriting uv's own accurate stderr — the misclassification the plan targets","scripts/check_uv_pin.py:364-380 already parses+validates the exact pin from pyproject.toml; a Makefile-side re-parse duplicates that logic","Context: uv 'correctly refused the mismatch' — so the swallowing catch-all, not a missing comparison, is the root cause"],"finding":"The Approach adds a bespoke Makefile preflight that re-parses `uv --version` and `[tool.uv] required-version` to compare them, but uv ITSELF already reads `required-version` and refuses a mismatch with a version-specific message; the real defect is that the venv recipe's catch-all (Makefile:200-208) swallows that message and reclassifies it as a missing interpreter. The plan does not weigh the lighter, structurally-different fix of surfacing / branching on uv's native mismatch stderr instead of re-implementing a version comparison.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8619b8c952ac9462","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Add a preflight that compares the selected uv executable/version with the repository exact required version before uv venv'","norm_id":"n7962c0716d64f559","priority":0.1711,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["uv output format for the mismatch message changes across uv releases, silently desyncing the hand-rolled Makefile parser from uv's actual behavior","A future contributor must maintain two independent version-comparison implementations (Makefile preflight + check_uv_pin.py)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the bespoke uv-version preflight against the lighter prior-art alternative of surfacing (not swallowing) uv's own `required-version` refusal — which already names the required and running versions — and explain why re-parsing/comparing is preferable to letting uv's native diagnostic through.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["pyproject.toml:353-354: `# NOTE: uv reads required-version itself, so a local uv that differs now fails fast with '# Update uv by running uv self update 0.12.7'. That is intended`","docs/local-dev-env.md:66-71 documents uv's own message: `error: Required uv version ==0.12.7 does not match the running version 0.7.18. Update uv by running uv self update 0.12.7.`","Makefile:200-208: the `uv venv --python ... || { ... }` handler SWALLOWS uv's stderr and substitutes the 'could not provision .venv on Python' / 'uv python install' message — the actual defect is the swallowing catch-all, not the absence of a version comparator","Web (astral-sh/uv issue #17609, dependabot-core #13199): uv commands fail with `error: Required uv version ==X does not match the running version Y` before running, confirming uv already provides the mismatch-specific diagnostic the plan proposes to build"],"finding":"The Approach reinvents uv's native `[tool.uv] required-version` enforcement — which already emits a precise, self-describing mismatch error naming required and running versions — instead of considering the lighter alternative of surfacing that existing error; the plan never mentions this prior art or justifies the bespoke reimplementation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff1256d9c1b1a8eb7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section (\"Add a preflight that compares the selected uv executable/version with the repository exact required version before `uv venv`\")","norm_id":"nff6456958cb84c98","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future uv version changes the `required-version` comparison/normalization semantics (e.g. specifier syntax), and the bespoke preflight's hand-rolled comparison drifts from uv's actual acceptance rule, reintroducing a mis-diagnosis.","The mismatch diagnostic the plan writes duplicates wording uv already prints, risking divergence from uv's own 'uv self update' remedy."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Approach, evaluate two options: (a) restructure the `uv venv` catch-all so uv's own `required-version` refusal (`error: Required uv version ... does not match the running version ...`) propagates unmasked, reserving the 'Python unavailable' message for genuine interpreter failures; vs (b) the proposed bespoke preflight. If (b) is chosen, state why (e.g. need for a repo-specific message) and pin the comparison to uv's own specifier semantics to avoid drift.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"sever